[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288760676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110496#issuecomment-3288760676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110496","id":3288760676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EBoFk","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-13T19:32:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-13T19:32:45Z","body":"Notice the weird width of the editor in the image of the issue description.\n\nNot only it's the issue underlined by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110495, but it seems to be even worse. Maybe the screen minimum width is linked once to the system scale (it would make sense), but never refreshed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288760676/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288803051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110496#issuecomment-3288803051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110496","id":3288803051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EBybr","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-13T20:20:44Z","updated_at":"2025-09-13T20:21:47Z","body":"As discussed on RocketChat, it looks like this isn't a Wayland-only issue unfortunately.\n\nThe minimum size is properly respected (1024x600), the issue is that it's just hardcoded by the editor.\n\nI could replicate this on X11 and it looks like this happens on Windows too, according to #102359. Since that issue is older, I'm closing this as a duplicate.\n\nThank you for reporting anyways, I really appreciate :D","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288803051/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288803588","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110496#issuecomment-3288803588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110496","id":3288803588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EBykE","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-13T20:21:29Z","updated_at":"2025-09-13T20:22:49Z","body":"Oops wrong issue 😅 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288803588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288841909","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110496#issuecomment-3288841909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110496","id":3288841909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EB761","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-13T20:52:29Z","updated_at":"2025-09-13T20:52:29Z","body":"Thank you for reporting!\n\nI've taken a look and it looks like there are multiple things at play.\n\nFirst of all, regarding the dynamic scale issue, the theme itself can't change at runtime yet, it's a limitation of the engine itself. IIRC the fix will eventually come as something like #86022, but it's not easy stuff from what I can tell.\n\nI guess we could try to mark the window as 2x scaled anyways, so that at least the result is uniform across displays (at the cost of a higher graphic workload). Not sure if that would cause issues with fractional scaling though.\n\nRegarding the funky window size, I'm not exactly sure what's going on either. I can replicate this on sway, but I wonder if this behavior might be left to the compositor to decide.\n\n> Maybe the screen minimum width is linked once to the system scale (it would make sense), but never refreshed.\n\nI thought this too (as discussed on RocketChat) but apparently I was wrong, it looks like the units used by the `set_min_size` and `set_max_size` are \"logical\" units, which are scale-independent, as with the rest of the protocol really. Kinda forgot about that 😅 \n\nOverall I'd say that this is quite complicated and would require further research and analysis. I'd rather work on this once we reach greater feature parity, once we add game embedding and other missing features.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3288841909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]